  "comment": "Real syft 1.46.0 output (SPDX 2.3), unedited, from a scan of a minimal npm project whose package-lock.json declares a git devDependency. The project is synthetic; the SBOM is not, so the field semantics and relationship orientation are the generator's. Purpose: the graph-root rule must lift NOTHING here. gitdep arrives versionless (a git ref carries no version) and has a transitive dependency of its own, so it satisfies the no-version, has-a-dependant and is-not-a-dependency clauses; only the golang clause keeps it. Removing that clause deletes a real component, which is the regression this file exists to catch and which no other real sample in this repo can. A hand-written fixture cannot serve the purpose because it would encode the same assumption the parser does."
